706:     ///
707:     /// Can we force Serde to call the typed methods (`deserialize_u8`, `deserialize_bool`, ...)?
708:     /// - Not from within a format Deserializer. Serde chooses which method to call based on the
709:     ///   Rust type information it has via the caller’s `Deserialize`/`DeserializeSeed` logic.
710:     ///   Implementing the typed methods (which we do) ensures Serde will use them whenever it knows
711:     ///   the target type; otherwise, it falls back to `deserialize_any`.
712:     ///
713:     /// Can we learn the target field’s Rust type from here?
714:     /// - No. Serde does not expose type reflection to Deserializers. The only hint we get is which
